        "id": 1409599
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-13T13:13:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I hope FUSE-BPF will make these patches obsolete.\n\nMaybe a solution to mitigate the warning would be to create two separate ioctl definitions under `#ifdef __KERNEL__`, but that would be ugly and probably not worth it...",
      "parentUuid": "0a4aacdd_703622d6",
      "revId": "92e19ce6cc059b74206b6fa53eeb2d705345da5c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cddd5404_99724674",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1869395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-14T23:30:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Also, if we want to combine both types `__u*` and `uint*_t`, we could _always_ include `linux/types.h`. Which is fine since we don\u0027t care about !__linux__. And this would also get rid of the warning. e.g.\n\n```\ndiff --git a/include/uapi/linux/fuse.h b/include/uapi/linux/fuse.h\nindex 84ba1d043d19..1bdd38e04851 100644\n--- a/include/uapi/linux/fuse.h\n+++ b/include/uapi/linux/fuse.h\n@@ -199,9 +199,8 @@\n #ifndef _LINUX_FUSE_H\n #define _LINUX_FUSE_H\n \n-#ifdef __KERNEL__\n #include \u003clinux/types.h\u003e\n-#else\n+#ifndef __KERNEL__\n #include \u003cstdint.h\u003e\n #endif\n\n```\n\nOther upstream uapi header already do this anyway.",
      "parentUuid": "5317f776_6708bf3e",
      "revId": "92e19ce6cc059b74206b6fa53eeb2d705345da5c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
